      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n3\\,\\sin\\left(56.25^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(56.25^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(112.5^\\circ\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=56.25^\\circ$ and then at $x=112.5^\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(112.5^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(112.5^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right)=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{8}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
